title{Cydon | A lightweight MVVM library based on Web Components}*
.fixed.top-4.right-4.z-9
	a.btn.btn-sm.btn-ghost[href=./index_zh.html]{中文}
.hero.bg-base-200
	.hero-content.flex-col.lg:flex-row
		img.rounded-lg.shadow-2xl.mr-8[src="./img/example.svg" title="code example"]
		div
			h1.text-5xl.font-bold{Cydon}
			p.text-lg.py-6{A lightweight MVVM library based on Web Components}
			a.btn.btn-primary[href=./docs.html#/en/]{Learn Cydon}
				text-transform none
section
	.box
		.flex.justify-center
			strong{Lightweight}
		.icon{🚀}
		p{Under 600 lines of core code, only ~3KB after Brotli compression}
	.box
		.flex.justify-center
			strong{No Virtual DOM}
		.icon{🔩}
		p{Built on native Web Components, no virtual DOM, no special Devtools extension needed}
	.box
		.flex.justify-center
			strong{No Build Step}
		.icon{🔌}
		p{Works out of the box, no compilation required. Proxy-based reactivity with dynamic property tracking}
section
	.box
		.flex.justify-center
			strong{Separation of Concerns}
		.icon{🏹}
		p{Separate DOM structure from logic for easier maintenance}
	.box
		.flex.justify-center
			strong{Easy to Learn}
		.icon{🔧}
		p{Simple API design, no new syntax to learn, just Web Components knowledge needed}
	.box
		.flex.justify-center
			strong{Progressive Loading}
		.icon{🧰}
		p{Built-in directives support on-demand loading, no need to load all at once}
section
	.w-100.p-8
		p{Cydon introduces a novel approach to building web applications. Instead of relying on virtual DOM, it collects all mutable DOM parts during the binding phase, maintains a mapping from variable names to DOM parts, and updates the DOM asynchronously.}
		p{Unlike virtual DOM approaches, when updating the DOM, Cydon doesn't need to traverse the (v)DOM tree since mutable parts are already collected during binding. It simply updates the changed parts in order, giving Cydon significant advantages in both performance and bundle size.}
	.mockup-code
		pre[data-prefix="&#36;"]
			code{pnpm i cydon}